"""An onset effect: a response to the first token, extended over repetitions.

At that position, numbers, isolated punctuation, indentation, and programming
introducers tend negative; ordinary word pieces tend mildly positive. The
response continues while the document repeats its initial token, then stops.
The keyword spellings have separate fitted weights; this is not a code parser.
